# Testing

## The gate

`scripts/check.sh` is the only definition of "ready to commit". CI runs the same script.

| Step | Tool | Fails when |
|---|---|---|
| Lint | `ruff check` | any rule in `[tool.ruff.lint]` is violated (includes security rules `S`) |
| Format | `ruff format --check` | a file is not formatted |
| Types | `mypy` (`strict = true`) | any type error in `src/{{ package_name }}` |
| Size | `scripts/check_sizes.py` | a file is over 800 lines or a function over 50 (warns over 400 lines) |
| Secrets | `scripts/check_secrets.py` | key material is tracked, staged or untracked-but-not-ignored |
| Tests | `pytest --cov` | a test fails or coverage drops below {{ min_coverage }}% |

## Layout

```
tests/
├── conftest.py      # shared fixtures
├── unit/            # fast, no I/O; mirrors src/{{ package_name }}/
{% if is_service %}
├── integration/     # real adapters (database, queues); keep them hermetic
└── e2e/             # the whole app through its HTTP interface
{% endif %}
```

## Rules of thumb

- Arrange, act, assert. One behavior per test; name it for the behavior (`test_rejects_empty_name`).
- Parametrize instead of copy-pasting cases.
- Mock only at the boundary you do not own (network, clock, cloud). Do not mock your own code.
- Tests that need real external systems get `@pytest.mark.live`. They are skipped by default;
  run them on purpose with `uv run pytest -m live --no-cov`.
- Fixtures contain synthetic data only. Never commit real data or credentials.

## Commands

```bash
uv run pytest                          # everything not marked live, with coverage
uv run pytest tests/unit --no-cov      # one area, fast
uv run pytest -k name --no-cov         # one test
```
